 r←Test_Server_426(stopFlag batchFlag);⎕TRAP;html
⍝ The list of packages carries a canonical link, and the "tag" parameter is not part of it:
⍝ Assets/JS/package-list.js reads that one in the browser, so every "?tag=..." URL - and
⍝ every package row links to one per tag of that package - returns the very same page.
⍝ "group" is a different matter, because the server really does filter by it, so it stays.
⍝ A parameter that cannot be expressed in the canonical link leaves the page without one
⍝ rather than with an untrue one; "userCommand" stands in for those here.
 ⎕TRAP←(999 'C' '. ⍝ Deliberate error')(0 'N')
 r←T._Failed

 html←∆GetHtmlFromServer'[localhost]/v1/packages'
 →T.PassesIf∨/'<link rel="canonical" href="/v1/packages">'⍷html

 html←∆GetHtmlFromServer'[localhost]/v1/packages?tag=files'
 →T.PassesIf∨/'<link rel="canonical" href="/v1/packages">'⍷html

 html←∆GetHtmlFromServer'[localhost]/v1/packages?group=example'
 →T.PassesIf∨/'<link rel="canonical" href="/v1/packages?group=example">'⍷html

 html←∆GetHtmlFromServer'[localhost]/v1/packages?group=example&tag=files'
 →T.PassesIf∨/'<link rel="canonical" href="/v1/packages?group=example">'⍷html

 html←∆GetHtmlFromServer'[localhost]/v1/packages/example-Goo'
 →T.PassesIf∨/'<link rel="canonical" href="/v1/packages/example-Goo">'⍷html

 html←∆GetHtmlFromServer'[localhost]/v1/packages?userCommand=1'
 →T.PassesIf~∨/'<link rel="canonical"'⍷html

 r←T._OK
⍝Done
